Let the blinking rate of the lighthouse be $r$ blinks per minute.
The light blinks 255 times in 5 minutes.
So, $r = \frac{255 \text{ blinks}}{5 \text{ minutes}} = 51 \text{ blinks per minute}$.

We want to find how long it takes the light to blink 459 times.
Let the time in minutes be $t$.
Then, the number of blinks in $t$ minutes is $r \times t$.
We want $r \times t = 459$.
Since $r = 51$, we have $51t = 459$.
Therefore, $t = \frac{459}{51} = 9$ minutes.

The light will take 9 minutes to blink 459 times.

We can set up a proportion:
$\frac{255 \text{ blinks}}{5 \text{ minutes}} = \frac{459 \text{ blinks}}{x \text{ minutes}}$
Cross-multiply: $255x = 5 \times 459$
$255x = 2295$
$x = \frac{2295}{255} = 9$
So it will take 9 minutes for the light to blink 459 times.

